---
description: frontend automated testing (Playwright E2E/L1, Vitest + React Testing Library; Jest only if not on Vite)
alwaysApply: false
---
Use when writing frontend automated tests. Pair with `testing.mdc` for level selection. Pair with `monorepo-architecture` when E2E runs against in-repo backends.

### Tooling

- E2E and integration L1: **Playwright**
- Unit: **Vitest** + **React Testing Library** (RTL) when the app is on **Vite** (the usual case for these rules). Use **Jest** + RTL only for non-Vite setups (or legacy apps that already standardize on Jest) — do not add Jest alongside Vite.
- Run locally via terminal (e.g. `npm test` / `npx vitest` / `npx playwright test`, or the project’s package scripts) as well as in CI — see `testing.mdc` Local runs.

### Layout (frontend package root)

```text
e2e/                         # Playwright: E2E and L1 specs
├── playwright.config.ts
├── fixtures/                # Optional: auth/storage helpers
└── ...
src/
└── **/__tests__/            # Or colocated *.test.ts(x) — Vitest + RTL (Jest + RTL only if not Vite)
```

### E2E

- Assert user-visible outcomes (roles, labels, text, navigation, results shown in the UI).
- Do not assert implementation details (specific HTML tags, CSS class soup, internal component structure).
- Frontend-only apps: no backend/seed setup required.
- Monorepo: point Playwright at the test stack (real backends + isolated data) — see `monorepo-architecture` and `testing.mdc`.

### Integration L1

- Same Playwright driver as E2E.
- Mock at the **network/service boundary** (e.g. Playwright route mocking) **only** for third parties that cannot be isolated in the test env.
- Keep the app and first-party backends real when they are part of the monorepo test stack.

### Unit (Vitest + RTL)

- Prefer testing single-job domain/helpers and presentational behavior with clear contracts (see `testing.mdc` — leaves, not orchestrating containers).
- Query by role, label, or text. Avoid asserting internal React state or child component structure.
- Do not unit-test multi-step container orchestration with heavy mocks of every collaborator — cover that with E2E/L1 (or L2 on the backend).
- Configure Vitest to align with the Vite app (same resolve aliases, etc.) so imports match production.
